-- `Ref` is the sole uppercase-named mutable-cell allocator (an extern FUNCTION,
-- not a data constructor).  Generalizing `Ref x` would be unsound (write at one
-- type, read at another).  This binding must NOT generalize — using it at two
-- incompatible types must error.  The exclusion in isCtorAppSpine is by the name
-- "Ref", so it works whether Ref is declared locally or comes from the prelude.
extern Ref : a -> Ref a
r = Ref (x => x)
-- Using r at two different function types in one tuple must produce a type error.
pair = ((r : Ref (Int -> Int)), (r : Ref (String -> String)))
